### Telecom middleware — every endpoint, in the order a real case uses them.
#
# Needs the REST Client extension (humao.rest-client). Click "Send Request" above any
# block, or put the cursor in one and press Ctrl+Alt+R.
#
# The token comes from DEV_TOKEN in .env. Fill it in with the VS Code task
# "Mint a dev token", or from a terminal:
#
#   uv run --env-file .env python scripts/dev_token.py --write-env
#
# The API must be running: F5, "API: run (breakpoints work)".

@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:9000
@api = {{baseUrl}}/api/v1
@token = {{$dotenv DEV_TOKEN}}
# Proves which *service* is calling, as distinct from which person. Read straight from
# .env, so it matches TELECOM_MCP_BACKEND_API_KEY without anything being pasted here.
# Only checked when TELECOM_MW_SERVICE_AUTH is not 'unchecked'; harmless when it is.
@service = {{$dotenv TELECOM_MW_SERVICE_SHARED_SECRET}}
@cx = CX-1234
@otherCx = CX-5555

### Liveness — answers even when the database is down
GET {{baseUrl}}/healthz

### Readiness — consults the database, so this is the one that tells you it is wired up
GET {{baseUrl}}/readyz

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### The customer's own view. Needs a customer token.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### The passcode check the voice agent does first. Demo passcode: 4821
POST {{api}}/customers/{{cx}}/authenticate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Service-Authorization: Bearer {{service}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cx_id": "{{cx}}",
  "passcode": "4821"
}

### The same call with the wrong passcode — note it never says how many attempts remain
POST {{api}}/customers/{{cx}}/authenticate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Service-Authorization: Bearer {{service}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cx_id": "{{cx}}",
  "passcode": "0000"
}

### Account details
GET {{api}}/customers/{{cx}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Service-Authorization: Bearer {{service}}

### Active services
GET {{api}}/customers/{{cx}}/services?limit=5
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Service-Authorization: Bearer {{service}}

### Orders, newest first
GET {{api}}/customers/{{cx}}/orders?limit=5
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Service-Authorization: Bearer {{service}}

### Invoices. total_minor is pennies: 6300 is £63.00
GET {{api}}/customers/{{cx}}/invoices?limit=5
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Service-Authorization: Bearer {{service}}

### Network status for the customer's own area — the area comes from their service
### record, never from anything the caller sends
GET {{api}}/customers/{{cx}}/network
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Service-Authorization: Bearer {{service}}

### Someone else's account. 403, with wording that gives nothing away
GET {{api}}/customers/{{otherCx}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Service-Authorization: Bearer {{service}}

### No token at all. 401
GET {{api}}/customers/{{cx}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Writes. Every one needs an idempotency key.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Raise a ticket. 201 the first time
POST {{api}}/customers/{{cx}}/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Service-Authorization: Bearer {{service}}
Idempotency-Key: idem-vscode-ticket-0001
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cx_id": "{{cx}}",
  "category": "network",
  "subject": "Broadband keeps dropping",
  "description": "The connection drops every evening around eight.",
  "priority": "normal"
}

### Send that exact request again. 200, the same ticket_id, deduplicated: true.
### One ticket exists, not two.
POST {{api}}/customers/{{cx}}/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Service-Authorization: Bearer {{service}}
Idempotency-Key: idem-vscode-ticket-0001
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cx_id": "{{cx}}",
  "category": "network",
  "subject": "Broadband keeps dropping",
  "description": "The connection drops every evening around eight.",
  "priority": "normal"
}

### The same key with different content. 409 — an error, not a silent replay of the
### wrong result
POST {{api}}/customers/{{cx}}/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Service-Authorization: Bearer {{service}}
Idempotency-Key: idem-vscode-ticket-0001
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cx_id": "{{cx}}",
  "category": "billing",
  "subject": "Something else entirely",
  "description": "A different request under a key that is already used.",
  "priority": "high"
}

### A write with no key at all. 422, naming the header it wanted
POST {{api}}/customers/{{cx}}/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Service-Authorization: Bearer {{service}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cx_id": "{{cx}}",
  "category": "billing",
  "subject": "No idempotency key",
  "description": "Refused before anything is written.",
  "priority": "low"
}

### The customer's tickets
GET {{api}}/customers/{{cx}}/tickets?limit=5
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Service-Authorization: Bearer {{service}}

### Book a callback. The time must carry a timezone offset
POST {{api}}/customers/{{cx}}/callbacks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Service-Authorization: Bearer {{service}}
Idempotency-Key: idem-vscode-callback-0001
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cx_id": "{{cx}}",
  "preferred_date": "2026-12-01T10:00:00+00:00",
  "window": "morning",
  "reason": "Discuss the outage credit"
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### The approval workflow. Nothing moves money.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Ask for a refund. 202, state pending, money_moved false.
### The evidence in the response is read from the invoice, not from the justification.
POST {{api}}/customers/{{cx}}/refund-approvals
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Service-Authorization: Bearer {{service}}
Idempotency-Key: idem-vscode-refund-0001
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cx_id": "{{cx}}",
  "invoice_id": "INV-2026-08",
  "amount_minor": 450,
  "currency": "GBP",
  "reason": "service_outage",
  "justification": "Broadband unavailable for three days in August."
}

### A refund larger than the invoice. 409
POST {{api}}/customers/{{cx}}/refund-approvals
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Service-Authorization: Bearer {{service}}
Idempotency-Key: idem-vscode-refund-0002
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cx_id": "{{cx}}",
  "invoice_id": "INV-2026-08",
  "amount_minor": 999999,
  "currency": "GBP",
  "reason": "goodwill",
  "justification": "More than the invoice was ever for."
}

### The supervisor's queue. 403 with a customer token — run the "Mint a dev token"
### task again and choose supervisor_approver, then send this.
GET {{api}}/approvals
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Service-Authorization: Bearer {{service}}

### Decide the one that came with the seed data. Needs the supervisor token.
POST {{api}}/approvals/APR-seed-0001/decision
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Service-Authorization: Bearer {{service}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "decision": "approved",
  "note": "Outage confirmed against incident INC-5512."
}

### Send that again. 409 — a decided request cannot be decided twice
POST {{api}}/approvals/APR-seed-0001/decision
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Service-Authorization: Bearer {{service}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "decision": "rejected",
  "note": "Second thoughts."
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### The other stakeholders
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Assign an account to an agent. Supervisor token.
POST {{api}}/assignments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Service-Authorization: Bearer {{service}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "agent_sub": "auth0|agent-7",
  "cx_id": "{{otherCx}}"
}

### What that agent may act on
GET {{api}}/assignments/auth0|agent-7
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Service-Authorization: Bearer {{service}}

### The audit trail, with the chain verified. Needs an admin_security token.
### Note cx_ref: a stable reference, never the customer's identifier.
GET {{api}}/audit?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Service-Authorization: Bearer {{service}}

### The live feed. Leave it running in one tab and send a write from another.
### Needs a token with case:read; a supervisor also sees approval events.
GET {{api}}/stream
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Service-Authorization: Bearer {{service}}
Accept: text/event-stream

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Voice case state — what makes a dropped call resumable
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Record a turn
PUT {{api}}/cases
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Service-Authorization: Bearer {{service}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cx_id": "{{cx}}",
  "case_id": "CASE-vscode-0001",
  "status": "active",
  "consent_recorded": true,
  "step": {
    "intent": "Ask about the August bill",
    "tool": "get_invoice_summary",
    "outcome": "answered"
  }
}

### The line drops
PUT {{api}}/cases
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Service-Authorization: Bearer {{service}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cx_id": "{{cx}}",
  "case_id": "CASE-vscode-0001",
  "status": "interrupted"
}

### They call back and re-authenticate. The case comes back with its steps intact,
### rather than starting again from nothing.
POST {{api}}/customers/{{cx}}/cases/resume
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Service-Authorization: Bearer {{service}}


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Which service is calling — only meaningful when TELECOM_MW_SERVICE_AUTH is set
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### A caller the API does not recognise. 401 service_not_recognised, even though the
### user token is perfectly valid — which is what makes a stolen token worth nothing
### replayed from somewhere else.
GET {{api}}/customers/{{cx}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Service-Authorization: Bearer not-the-configured-credential

### The same request with the header left off entirely. 401, but
### service_credential_missing, and the body names the header. Sending nothing is a
### configuration mistake; sending the wrong thing is the case above, and only that one
### stays opaque.
GET {{api}}/customers/{{cx}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### No service credential at all. Same refusal.
GET {{api}}/customers/{{cx}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### A recognised service with no user token. 401 unauthenticated — the service
### credential authenticates the robot, never the person.
GET {{api}}/customers/{{cx}}
X-Service-Authorization: Bearer {{service}}
